---
import Base from '@layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { changelog } from '@lib/changelog';
const projects = (await getCollection('projects')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const entries = changelog;
---
<Base title="Changelog">
  <h1>Changelog</h1>
  <p class="lede">What changed on the site and in the pipelines. Data refreshes are not listed; they run automatically and show up as "data as of" stamps on each page.</p>
  <ul class="log">
    {entries.map((e) => (<li><time datetime={e.date}>{e.date}</time><span>{e.text}</span></li>))}
  </ul>
  <h2>Not built yet (deliberately)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Midterms v2 views: state-race heat table and volume/liquidity charts, plus Cook ratings as the baseline input (before election day).</li>
    <li>FOMC market-reaction leg (Treasury yields and equity moves on decision day versus the surprise): needs FRED and Tiingo keys.</li>
    <li>SaaS: per-company quarterly drill-down and an investor-relations spot check of three numbers per company.</li>
    <li>Personal portfolio attribution from a brokerage account: not published pending a decision on making it public.</li>
    <li>Tableau / Power BI export attachments of the same facts, resume link, custom domain.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Projects</h2>
  <ul>
    {projects.map((p) => (<li><a href={`/projects/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a> <span class="muted">· {p.data.status} · started {p.data.started}</span></li>))}
  </ul>
</Base>
